<<~ ahu slot=`#/glass-mirror-a-posiwid-reading-at-725c31b72`>>

! Glass mirror: a POSIWID reading at 725c31b72 (Fable scout, Glass-Reader, 2026-11-11)

Saved by the controller from the scout's hand-back. The harness refused the subagent's own write.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/short-reading`>>

!! Short reading
The page stacks two surfaces:
* `#mirror`: an in-page TW5 engine, the "glass mirror", at width full or skinny.
* `#projection`: the worker-rendered floor, width none, carrying `lar:frame` + `data-lar-rid`.

When the mirror shows, CSS hides `#projection`. The weld and the smoke's DOM probe both read the hidden floor.

| Observation | Verdict | Cause |h
| Pane "labelled &#64;daemon" | By design, misread | It is a summon BUTTON in the heading. Nothing names the shown wiki. |
| Unstyled TW5 | Unbuilt | No TW5 theme plugin (vanilla/snowwhite) ships in the genesis boot set. The core blob carries no `$:/themes/tiddlywiki/vanilla/base`. |
| Stock GettingStarted | Unbuilt, plus a boot-order gap | Core's shadow `$:/DefaultTiddlers` reads GettingStarted. No house override exists, and lar-story opens the story inside engine boot, before any record lands (tw5-vm-gaps-scout row 17). |

''Built:'' the mirror machinery. One door (`standMirror`), skinny then widen, one step down, crash records, the write road (`port:write`), no syncer/saver.

''Gaps:'' what the engine gets fed (theme, default story, palette pointer) and what the weld reads.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/canon-intent`>>

!! Canon intent
* `dreamdom.mem#/the-width-dial`: full → skinny → story → none.
* `d3-glass-lane.mem#/the-visible-mirror`: the mirror IS the surface. Default full, measured, never requested.
* Owed in canon: G3 doors (modal, notify, clipboard, download, route); G6 goldens 1–13 at full against stock TW5 (arc M2–M4).
* Canon is silent on theme/styling.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gap-table`>>

!! Gap table (abridged)
* ''Wired:'' mirror door; skinny/widen; step-down; crash records; mirror visible; edit road; no syncer.
* ''Partial:'' plugin gate on `sealedRest` (the feed never reaches inputs); G3 doors (only scroller, popup, focus).
* ''Absent:''
** stock theme blob;
** palette (boot shadows point `$:/palette` at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/lararium/palette/gruvbox-dark`, but the carrier titles itself `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/palette/gruvbox-dark`, and its type reads memetic-wikitext);
** house default story;
** pane names the shown wiki;
** goldens;
** weld reads the person's surface;
** node SSR projection (D6/D14).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/what-the-weld-would-need`>>

!! What the weld would need (tools/browser-weld/weld.mjs:75-92 drives the hidden #projection)
* Assert `data-lar-shown`, then drive `#mirror`'s shadow root with real input.
* Wait for the settle (`full`, or `skinny` with a named reason).
* ''Styled:'' a rule for `.tc-sidebar-scrollable`; computed `position: fixed` on the sidebar; toolbar SVG width bounded; a palette colour reaches the background.
* ''Content:'' the first story title equals the wiki's own `$:/DefaultTiddlers`, not GettingStarted.
* ''Editable:'' real edit, type, save, then read back from the WORKER.
* ''Label:'' the pane names the shown wiki, matching the vessel card.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/suggested-build-order`>>

!! Suggested build order (red first)
# The weld reads the mirror.
# The theme ships by CID (one blob class in build-genesis-island + bootSetPluginCids, read by worker and mirror alike).
# The palette pointer trues to the carrier title, and the carrier becomes a palette dictionary.
# The default story belongs to the wiki. The mirror opens its story after the port's first snapshot, never inside engine boot.
# The pane names its surface and carries the held-skinny reason.
# G3 doors.
# M4 goldens at full against stock.
# Isomorphic witness on a node fake-document camera, ahead of D6 SSR.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/uncertainties`>>

!! Uncertainties (scout's own)
* ''Inferred:'' the person saw the mirror while the probe read the floor; why it read skinny; the visual symptoms (not rendered).
* ''Not traced:'' who writes `$:/StoryList` in the worker.
* ''Tension:'' "no VM on the main thread" was re-read by the 2026-10-29 ruling as "no SOVEREIGN VM and no KEY on a surface". The mirror runs a whole engine on the page under that ruling.

Full hand-back text lives in the controller transcript (session eb8cf0a6), 2026-11-11.

<<~/ahu>>

